────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  SUMMARY
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Iteration 1 fully confirmed the core P/D disaggregation latency model: disaggregated (AD) mode delivers lower inter-token latency than aggregated (AL) mode at every tested arrival rate (5–130 req/s), with the ITL gap growing monotonically from 0.06 ms to 1.68 ms as predicted. The tradeoff—AD incurs ~4–10 ms higher TTFT than AL—was also confirmed, with the gap narrowing at high load as anticipated by the paper's queueing model.

